* Smart Fan RevA - Buzzer Driver & Flyback Clamp Simulation
* Demonstrates S8050 saturation and inductive spike clamping with 1N4148

* Power Supplies
VCC 5V 0 DC 5.0

* MCU PB14 Pulse: 0V -> 3.3V, 50us ON, then turn OFF
VPB14 PB14 0 PULSE(0 3.3 0 10n 10n 50u 100u)

* ========================================================
* Circuit 1: PROTECTED (With 1N4148 Diode)
* ========================================================
RB1 PB14 BASE1 1k
RPD1 BASE1 0 10k
Q1 COLL_PROT BASE1 0 S8050
RBUZ1 5V N_BUZ1 100
LBUZ1 N_BUZ1 COLL_PROT 5m
D_CLAMP COLL_PROT 5V 1N4148

* ========================================================
* Circuit 2: UNPROTECTED (Without Diode - Dangerous Kickback)
* ========================================================
RB2 PB14 BASE2 1k
RPD2 BASE2 0 10k
Q2 COLL_UNPROT BASE2 0 S8050
RBUZ2 5V N_BUZ2 100
LBUZ2 N_BUZ2 COLL_UNPROT 5m
CPAR2 COLL_UNPROT 0 35p

* Device Models
.model S8050 NPN(IS=1e-14 BF=150 VAF=50 IKF=0.3 ISE=1e-12 NE=1.5 BR=4 CJC=10p CJE=25p TF=400p TR=50n)
.model 1N4148 D(IS=2.52n RS=0.568 N=1.752 CJO=4p TT=4n BV=100)

* Simulation Command: 120us transient with 10ns max timestep
.tran 0.1u 120u 0 10n

.backanno
.end
